## Styling Rules

- Use **Tailwind v4** utilities backed by `@theme` tokens — not inline styles except for animation initial states (see HeroSection).
- Scoped component styles go in `<style>` blocks within `.astro` files (Nav theme switch, writing page filters, pull quotes).
- Page-specific layout styles belong in the page's `<style>` block, not global CSS.
- IMPORTANT: Import `../styles/global.css` only from layouts — components rely on layout-level import.
- Use `class:list` for conditional classes in Astro (see `ArrowLink.astro`, `PhotoCard.astro`).
- Border radius on cards: `rounded-lg` (maps to `--radius-card` / 8px).
- Images: `loading="lazy"`, `decoding="async"`, responsive `srcset` via Sanity helpers in `lib/sanity.ts`.

---

## Component Patterns

- Export Astro components as default; define props with TypeScript `interface Props` in frontmatter.
- Accept optional `className` prop when the component needs composition (see `ArrowLink.astro`).
- Use **Material Icons** (`material-icons` class) for arrows and lightbox controls — do not add new icon libraries.
- Theme toggle: `role="switch"`, `aria-checked`, `aria-label` on the button in Nav.
- Dark mode: `document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', 'dark')` — tokens swap automatically.
- Chat/lightbox overlays: prefer `color/overlay` token values over raw `bg-black/90`.

---

## Asset Handling

- IMPORTANT: If Figma MCP returns a localhost image/SVG URL, use it directly during development.
- Production assets live in `portfolio/public/` (e.g. `/animated_abstract_logo.lottie`).
- Sanity images: use `urlFor()` and `getResponsiveProps()` from `lib/sanity.ts`.
- Do not install new icon packages — Material Icons + inline SVGs only.

---

## Accessibility

- Interactive elements require `aria-label` or visible text.
- Color contrast: design tokens are validated for AA (Light + Dark) in Figma.
- Lightbox: `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, keyboard navigation (Escape, arrows).
- Nav links and filter tabs must be keyboard-focusable (`<a>` or `<button>`).

---

## What NOT to do

- Do not create duplicate components when a Figma component already maps to an existing `.astro` file.
- Do not hardcode colors, spacing, or font families outside the token system.
- Do not use `stone-*` / `gray-*` Tailwind colors for design-system UI (ChatAgent is a known exception to fix).
- Do not copy Figma MCP React output verbatim — translate to Astro + project conventions.
- Do not add React/Vue islands unless the feature requires client interactivity (prefer `<script>` in Astro for lightbox, chat, theme).

---

## Validation Checklist

Before completing any Figma-driven change:

- [ ] `get_design_context` + `get_screenshot` were used
- [ ] Existing component reused or extended when mapping exists
- [ ] Colors use semantic tokens (`text-primary`, `text-muted`, `bg-surface`, etc.)
- [ ] Typography matches the Figma text style mapping table
- [ ] Spacing uses `spacing/section`, `spacing/block`, or `spacing/inline` scale
- [ ] Dark mode verified with `[data-theme="dark"]`
- [ ] Visual parity checked against Figma screenshot
